      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "HFS hierarchical feature selection (cv2.hfs)\n\nSegments the image into regions by merging SLIC superpixels along a texton + colour gradient criterion (two stages). 'CV HFS Segmentation' outputs a uint16 per-pixel region index map ('labels'), a region-coloured repaint of the image (each region = its average colour), and the region count.\n\nTry raising 'egb thresholds' to merge more aggressively, or lowering 'min region sizes'; lower 'spatial weight' to let colour/texture dominate. Runs on CPU - no GPU needed. The input image must be copied from example_inputs/water_coins.jpg into ComfyUI/input."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
